    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{4}{15}$.\n\nUse the limiting-sum formula for the whole series and the even-indexed terms; these give $r=\\dfrac35$.",
      "worked": "Let $a$ be the first term and $r$ the common ratio, with $|r|<1$. The even-indexed terms have first term $ar$ and common ratio $r^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a}{1-r}&=\\frac23\\\\\\frac{ar}{1-r^2}&=\\frac14.\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing $1-r^2=(1-r)(1+r)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac14&=\\frac{a}{1-r}\\frac{r}{1+r}\\\\\\frac14&=\\frac{2r}{3(1+r)}\\\\3(1+r)&=8r\\\\3&=5r\\\\r&=\\frac35.\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac23(1-r)\\\\a&=\\frac23\\left(1-\\frac35\\right)\\\\a&=\\frac4{15}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
